/* THE LEAF DENYLIST — command leaves that may NEVER be hot-swappable,
 * for a reason no generic eligibility check can express.
 *
 * Consumer must define:
 *   HOTSWAP_DENIED_LEAF(leaf, reason)
 *
 * `leaf`   the canonical dotted command-leaf path, exactly as declared in the
 *          engine/composition/commands catalog.
 * `reason` one line, present tense, saying what a swapped generation of that
 *          leaf could misreport. The reason lives HERE, next to the name, on
 *          purpose: a bare list of strings in a shell script is a list nobody
 *          can defend, and the next lane deletes it as unexplained.
 *
 * ── WHY A SECOND, LEAF-LEVEL LIST EXISTS ───────────────────────────────────
 * engine/composition/hotswap_eligible.def and engine/composition/hotswap_swappable.def are ALLOWLISTS
 * of translation units, and check-hotswap-eligible-scope /
 * check-hotswap-swappable-shape police them by PATH: nothing under core/,
 * lib/consensus/, core/modules/validation/, engine/modules/storage/, core/modules/net/, core/modules/coins/ or
 * engine/jobs/ may ever appear. That root check cannot express the rule below,
 * because the owning TU here is engine/controllers/src/chain_native_handlers.c —
 * a legitimately eligible app-layer controller that is ALREADY admitted today
 * (probe core.consensus.utxo.audit). What has to be denied is two LEAF NAMES
 * inside an otherwise-eligible file, not a path.
 *
 * Nor does "READY + read-only" express it. Both leaves below are
 * ZCL_COMMAND_READY_READ and would pass every existing eligibility gate
 * cleanly. That is exactly the problem: they RENDER BLOCK AND TRANSACTION
 * BYTES. A swapped renderer misreports chain data to every reader on the RPC
 * surface — wallets, explorers, other nodes' operators — without touching one
 * line of validation, and the node's own consensus state stays perfectly
 * consistent while it lies about what it holds. "Read-only" is not the right
 * test on a rendering path; "does a caller treat this output as the chain
 * itself" is.
 *
 * Until 2026-08-26 these two were merely NOT LISTED anywhere, which is an
 * accident rather than a decision: a future lane that passed the generic
 * checks could have admitted them and no gate would have objected. This file
 * is the decision, and check-hotswap-denied-leaves is its enforcement.
 *
 * ── HOW IT IS ENFORCED ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 * check-hotswap-denied-leaves (make lint; --selftest proves it fires on a
 * seeded fixture) refuses if any leaf below appears as a quoted token in ANY
 * hot-swap manifest — engine/composition/hotswap_eligible.def probes,
 * engine/composition/hotswap_swappable.def leaf lists, engine/composition/hotswap_probe_cases.def
 * operations, engine/composition/hotswap_services.def probe leaves, and every other
 * config/hotswap*.def / engine/composition/hotfork_capsules.def, including ones added
 * after this file was written. The gate fails CLOSED: a missing, unreadable
 * or empty denylist is exit 2, never "nothing is denied".
 *
 * It also scans the manifest that is written in C. The Tier-1 generation path
 * stages whatever a TU's ZCL_HOTSWAP_EXPORT_LEAVES table exports and
 * hotswap_leaf_stage_thunk() (engine/modules/hotswap/src/hotswap_loader.c) applies NO
 * per-leaf allowlist, so both leaves below were being re-pointed by a
 * recompiled generation of engine/controllers/src/chain_native_handlers.c while
 * appearing in no .def at all. That is the state this file was written into,
 * and the gate found it. The two trampolines are gone; the audit leaf remains.
 *
 * ── ADDING OR REMOVING A ROW ───────────────────────────────────────────────
 * Adding: state the misreport in the reason. Removing: a row here encodes an
 * OWNER decision, not a lint preference. Do not delete one to unblock a lane.
 *
 * Keep this DATA ONLY (no C tokens beyond the macro invocations). */

HOTSWAP_DENIED_LEAF("core.chain.block.get",
    "Renders a full block record (header + transactions) from the local block "
    "index; a swapped renderer misreports chain contents to every RPC reader "
    "without touching validation.")

HOTSWAP_DENIED_LEAF("core.chain.transaction.get",
    "Renders decoded transaction fields and bounded raw_hex pages from mempool "
    "or the block index; a swapped renderer misreports transaction bytes a "
    "caller treats as authoritative, again with validation untouched.")
